# Screenshots / images in root.
# Anchored with a leading slash so they match the ROOT only, which is what the
# comment above always said. Unanchored, `*.png` matches at any depth and was
# silently swallowing src/assets/ -- a component could import an image, build
# fine locally, and break for everyone else because the asset never left the
# machine it was added on.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg

# Screenshot directories. These were previously caught by the unanchored
# `*.png` above; anchoring it to the root released them, so they are named
# here instead. They are captured evidence -- audit runs, review shots -- and
# are regenerated on demand, unlike src/assets/ which the app imports at build
# time. That is the whole distinction the old rule could not express.
_docs/screenshots/
_review_shots/
_review/**/shots/
__MACOSX/


